@anon.faf009aaacdb3bbda30f9435f6d39aa4.1425 = private unnamed_addr constant [976 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for the use of hardcoded temporary file or directory paths.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AThe use of hardcoded paths for temporary files can be insecure. If an\0Aattacker discovers the location of a hardcoded path, they can replace the\0Acontents of the file or directory with a malicious payload.\0A\0AOther programs may also read or write contents to these hardcoded paths,\0Acausing unexpected behavior.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Awith open(\22/tmp/foo.txt\22, \22w\22) as file:\0A    ...\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Aimport tempfile\0A\0Awith tempfile.NamedTemporaryFile() as file:\0A    ...\0A```\0A\0A## Options\0A- `lint.flake8-bandit.hardcoded-tmp-directory`\0A- `lint.flake8-bandit.hardcoded-tmp-directory-extend`\0A\0A## References\0A- [Common Weakness Enumeration: CWE-377](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/377.html)\0A- [Common Weakness Enumeration: CWE-379](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/379.html)\0A- [Python documentation: `tempfile`](https://docs.python.org/3/library/tempfile.html)\0A", align 1
