@anon.faf009aaacdb3bbda30f9435f6d39aa4.1446 = private unnamed_addr constant [684 x i8] c"## What it does\0ACheck for method calls that initiate a subprocess with a shell.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AStarting a subprocess with a shell can allow attackers to execute arbitrary\0Ashell commands. Consider starting the process without a shell call and\0Asanitize the input to mitigate the risk of shell injection.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Aimport subprocess\0A\0Asubprocess.run(\22ls -l\22, shell=True)\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Aimport subprocess\0A\0Asubprocess.run([\22ls\22, \22-l\22])\0A```\0A\0A## References\0A- [Python documentation: `subprocess` \E2\80\94 Subprocess management](https://docs.python.org/3/library/subprocess.html)\0A- [Common Weakness Enumeration: CWE-78](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/78.html)\0A", align 1
