@anon.faf009aaacdb3bbda30f9435f6d39aa4.1495 = private unnamed_addr constant [547 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for uses of `datetime.datetime.min` and `datetime.datetime.max`.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0A`datetime.min` and `datetime.max` are non-timezone-aware datetime objects.\0A\0AAs such, operations on `datetime.min` and `datetime.max` may behave\0Aunexpectedly, as in:\0A\0A```python\0A# Timezone: UTC-14\0Adatetime.min.timestamp()  # ValueError: year 0 is out of range\0Adatetime.max.timestamp()  # ValueError: year 10000 is out of range\0A```\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Adatetime.max\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Adatetime.max.replace(tzinfo=datetime.UTC)\0A```\0A", align 1
