@anon.faf009aaacdb3bbda30f9435f6d39aa4.1566 = private unnamed_addr constant [932 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for module-level imports that should instead be imported lazily\0A(e.g., within a function definition, or an `if TYPE_CHECKING:` block, or\0Asome other nested context).\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0ASome modules are expensive to import. For example, importing `torch` or\0A`tensorflow` can introduce a noticeable delay in the startup time of a\0APython program.\0A\0AIn such cases, you may want to enforce that the module is imported lazily\0Aas needed, rather than at the top of the file. This could involve inlining\0Athe import into the function that uses it, rather than importing it\0Aunconditionally, to ensure that the module is only imported when necessary.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Aimport tensorflow as tf\0A\0A\0Adef show_version():\0A    print(tf.__version__)\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Adef show_version():\0A    import tensorflow as tf\0A\0A    print(tf.__version__)\0A```\0A\0A## Options\0A- `lint.flake8-tidy-imports.banned-module-level-imports`\0A", align 1
