@anon.faf009aaacdb3bbda30f9435f6d39aa4.1700 = private unnamed_addr constant [624 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for custom exception definitions that omit the `Error` suffix.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AThe `Error` suffix is recommended by [PEP 8]:\0A\0A> Because exceptions should be classes, the class naming convention\0A> applies here. However, you should use the suffix `\22Error\22` on your\0A> exception names (if the exception actually is an error).\0A\0A## Example\0A\0A```python\0Aclass Validation(Exception): ...\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A\0A```python\0Aclass ValidationError(Exception): ...\0A```\0A\0A## Options\0A- `lint.pep8-naming.ignore-names`\0A- `lint.pep8-naming.extend-ignore-names`\0A\0A[PEP 8]: https://peps.python.org/pep-0008/#exception-names\0A", align 1
