@anon.faf009aaacdb3bbda30f9435f6d39aa4.1741 = private unnamed_addr constant [568 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for invalid escape sequences.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AInvalid escape sequences are deprecated in Python 3.6.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Aregex = \22\\.png$\22\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Aregex = r\22\\.png$\22\0A```\0A\0AOr, if the string already contains a valid escape sequence:\0A```python\0Avalue = \22new line\\nand invalid escape \\_ here\22\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Avalue = \22new line\\nand invalid escape \\\\_ here\22\0A```\0A\0A## References\0A- [Python documentation: String and Bytes literals](https://docs.python.org/3/reference/lexical_analysis.html#string-and-bytes-literals)\0A", align 1
