@anon.faf009aaacdb3bbda30f9435f6d39aa4.1775 = private unnamed_addr constant [1084 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for multi-line docstrings whose closing quotes are not on their\0Aown line.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0A[PEP 257] recommends that the closing quotes of a multi-line docstring be\0Aon their own line, for consistency and compatibility with documentation\0Atools that may need to parse the docstring.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Adef sort_list(l: List[int]) -> List[int]:\0A    \22\22\22Return a sorted copy of the list.\0A\0A    Sort the list in ascending order and return a copy of the result using the\0A    bubble sort algorithm.\22\22\22\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Adef sort_list(l: List[int]) -> List[int]:\0A    \22\22\22Return a sorted copy of the list.\0A\0A    Sort the list in ascending order and return a copy of the result using the bubble\0A    sort algorithm.\0A    \22\22\22\0A```\0A\0A## References\0A- [PEP 257 \E2\80\93 Docstring Conventions](https://peps.python.org/pep-0257/)\0A- [NumPy Style Guide](https://numpydoc.readthedocs.io/en/latest/format.html)\0A- [Google Python Style Guide - Docstrings](https://google.github.io/styleguide/pyguide.html#38-comments-and-docstrings)\0A\0A[PEP 257]: https://peps.python.org/pep-0257/\0A", align 1
