@anon.faf009aaacdb3bbda30f9435f6d39aa4.1783 = private unnamed_addr constant [1021 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for docstring first lines that are not in an imperative mood.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0A[PEP 257] recommends that the first line of a docstring be written in the\0Aimperative mood, for consistency.\0A\0AHint: to rewrite the docstring in the imperative, phrase the first line as\0Aif it were a command.\0A\0AThis rule may not apply to all projects; its applicability is a matter of\0Aconvention. By default, this rule is enabled when using the `numpy` and\0A`pep257` conventions, and disabled when using the `google` conventions.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Adef average(values: list[float]) -> float:\0A    \22\22\22Returns the mean of the given values.\22\22\22\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Adef average(values: list[float]) -> float:\0A    \22\22\22Return the mean of the given values.\22\22\22\0A```\0A\0A## Options\0A- `lint.pydocstyle.convention`\0A- `lint.pydocstyle.property-decorators`\0A- `lint.pydocstyle.ignore-decorators`\0A\0A## References\0A- [PEP 257 \E2\80\93 Docstring Conventions](https://peps.python.org/pep-0257/)\0A\0A[PEP 257]: https://peps.python.org/pep-0257/\0A", align 1
