@anon.faf009aaacdb3bbda30f9435f6d39aa4.1802 = private unnamed_addr constant [891 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks duplicate characters in `str.strip` calls.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AAll characters in `str.strip` calls are removed from both the leading and\0Atrailing ends of the string. Including duplicate characters in the call\0Ais redundant and often indicative of a mistake.\0A\0AIn Python 3.9 and later, you can use `str.removeprefix` and\0A`str.removesuffix` to remove an exact prefix or suffix from a string,\0Arespectively, which should be preferred when possible.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0A# Evaluates to \22foo\22.\0A\22bar foo baz\22.strip(\22bar baz \22)\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0A# Evaluates to \22foo\22.\0A\22bar foo baz\22.strip(\22abrz \22)  # \22foo\22\0A```\0A\0AOr:\0A```python\0A# Evaluates to \22foo\22.\0A\22bar foo baz\22.removeprefix(\22bar \22).removesuffix(\22 baz\22)\0A```\0A\0A## Options\0A- `target-version`\0A\0A## References\0A- [Python documentation: `str.strip`](https://docs.python.org/3/library/stdtypes.html?highlight=strip#str.strip)\0A", align 1
