@anon.faf009aaacdb3bbda30f9435f6d39aa4.1817 = private unnamed_addr constant [438 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for hard-coded sequence accesses that are known to be out of bounds.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AAttempting to access a sequence with an out-of-bounds index will cause an\0A`IndexError` to be raised at runtime. When the sequence and index are\0Adefined statically (e.g., subscripts on `list` and `tuple` literals, with\0Ainteger indexes), such errors can be detected ahead of time.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Aprint([0, 1, 2][3])\0A```\0A", align 1
