@anon.faf009aaacdb3bbda30f9435f6d39aa4.1839 = private unnamed_addr constant [396 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for uses of the Unicode kind prefix (`u`) in strings.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AIn Python 3, all strings are Unicode by default. The Unicode kind prefix is\0Aunnecessary and should be removed to avoid confusion.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Au\22foo\22\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0A\22foo\22\0A```\0A\0A## References\0A- [Python documentation: Unicode HOWTO](https://docs.python.org/3/howto/unicode.html)\0A", align 1
