@anon.faf009aaacdb3bbda30f9435f6d39aa4.1868 = private unnamed_addr constant [542 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for invalid use of literals in assert message arguments.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AAn assert message which is a non-string literal was likely intended\0Ato be used in a comparison assertion, rather than as a message.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Afruits = [\22apples\22, \22plums\22, \22pears\22]\0Afruits.filter(lambda fruit: fruit.startwith(\22p\22))\0Aassert len(fruits), 2  # True unless the list is empty\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Afruits = [\22apples\22, \22plums\22, \22pears\22]\0Afruits.filter(lambda fruit: fruit.startwith(\22p\22))\0Aassert len(fruits) == 2\0A```\0A", align 1
